    "email": {
      "subject": "FW: FNOL: Lone Star Freight Systems LP \u2013 Policy CA-9948120 \u2013 Vehicle Damage and Third-Party Property Claim",
      "body": "Good afternoon,\n\nPlease treat this message as the first notice of loss for Lone Star Freight Systems LP under policy CA-9948120 with Great West Casualty Company.\n\nIncident summary: On 03/11/2026 at approximately 7:25 a.m. CST, one of the insured\u2019s tractors was involved in a backing loss at a customer dock in Grand Prairie, TX, resulting in damage to the company vehicle and reported impact to a dock door and loading barrier. No injuries have been reported at this time.\n\nPlease open a claim and advise the claim number, adjuster assignment, and any immediate next steps. We are also requesting confirmation that the loss will be handled on the current policy effective 03/15/2026.\n\nNamed insured: Lone Star Freight Systems LP\nPolicy number: CA-9948120\n\nThank you,\nWade Carrington\nLone Star Freight Systems LP\n\nCorrection: the total premium should read slightly lower than the attached invoice; we're reconciling.\n\nOn Mon, Jul 6, 2026 at 9:14 AM, Mia Salazar <trucking@swtransins.com> wrote:\n> Thanks for sending this over \u2014 can you confirm the requested effective date and whether any additional insureds are needed?\n>\n> Regards,\n> Mia Salazar",
      "sender": "Mia Salazar's Assistant <assistant@greatwestcasualty.com> on behalf of Wade Carrington <wcarrington@lonestarfreight.com>",
      "recipient": "claims@greatwestcasualty.com, underwriting@greatwestcasualty.com"
    },
